      "seed": 366349,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 839703,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "Bus Write Communication Cycle",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "flow-mu42zdxy-10"
    },
    {
      "id": "sub-mu42zdxy-6-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -651,
      "y": 311,
      "width": 275,
      "height": 190,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42zdy2_1"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 445170,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 26690,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "Every computer program reduces to\nfour basic external bus cycles:\nMemory Read (IO/M'=0, RD'=0, WR'=1)\nto fetch opcodes and operands;\nMemory Write (IO/M'=0, RD'=1,\nWR'=0) to store results; I/O Read\n(IO/M'=1, RD'=0, WR'=1) to accept\ndata from sensors/ports; and I/O\nWrite (IO/M'=1, RD'=1, WR'=0) to\noutput data to actuators/displays.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "edge-sub-mu42zdxy-6-sub-mu42zdxy-6-note",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "flow-mu42zdxy-8-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -485,
      "y": 538,
      "width": 314,
      "height": 114,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42zdy2_1"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 517399,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 995965,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "The microprocessor places a 16-bit\naddress on the address bus to select the\ntargeted memory location or I/O port via\naddress decoders, asserts the active-low\nRD' strobe, and latches data driven onto\nD7-D0 into internal registers.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "edge-flow-mu42zdxy-8-flow-mu42zdxy-8-note",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "flow-mu42zdxy-10-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 403,
      "width": 314,
      "height": 95,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42zdy2_1"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 96220,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 424867,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "The CPU asserts the targeted 16-bit\naddress, drives computed data onto data\nbus lines D7-D0, and emits an active-low\nWR' strobe pulse to latch the data byte\npermanently into the external device.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "edge-flow-mu42zdxy-10-flow-mu42zdxy-10-note",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ]
    },
